WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Trace an API request. Open Dev Tools > Request logs. This walkthrough uses fictional demo activity.

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:10.000
Focus on Needs attention. Use the view to find requests that need investigation, then open a row.

3
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:18.000
Read status and troubleshooting. This example returned HTTP 429. Respect Retry-After and keep the same key for a retry of the same write.

4
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:23.000
Inspect the response summary. Logs retain safe metadata, not full request or response bodies. Use Data Lookup for payload examples.

5
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Review Activity. Keep the request ID and UTC timestamp with your client-side trace.

6
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:33.000
Return to the list. Closing the drawer does not resend the request.

7
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Use Errors & retries. Select Needs attention to focus on failures. A missing error code is not a successful response.
